# Lost Jitte is charged on turn 3 by an unblocked Basking Rootwalla. Bot2 puts two Ornithopters onto the battlefield on
# turn 4. On turn 5 Bot1 removes the charge for "target creature can't block this turn", aimed at the first
# Ornithopter, then attacks: that Ornithopter may not block (the refusal) and the other may (the control), and the
# Rootwalla's damage to the blocker charges the Jitte again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Basking Rootwalla
Lost Jitte
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x2
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Basking Rootwalla.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lost Jitte.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Lost Jitte.Activate(Ability: Equip; Basking Rootwalla)
Bot1.Attack(Basking Rootwalla > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Lost Jitte.Counters.Charge = 1
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Lost Jitte.Activate(Ability: Remove)
Bot1.Modes(Target creature can't block this turn.)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Lost Jitte.Counters.Charge = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Basking Rootwalla > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Basking Rootwalla)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#2 > Basking Rootwalla)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Lost Jitte.Counters.Charge = 1

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Damage = 1
